      "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nPrevent background data-loader pinning from invalidating optimizer CUDA graph capture by setting `capture_error_mode=\"thread_local\"`, matching `FullCudaGraphWrapper`.\n\nDuring the first optimizer capture (step 4 with three warmup steps), a DataLoader pinning thread can need a fresh `cudaHostAlloc` for a future batch. The optimizer wrapper currently inherits PyTorch's `global` capture mode. In the controlled reproduction, the background allocation returns `cudaErrorStreamCaptureUnsupported` (900), invalidates capture, and causes the training thread to fail with an invalidated-capture allocator assertion or error 901.\n\n`thread_local` is appropriate because the background allocation is pinned **CPU** memory for future input; the optimizer graph does not reference it or depend on its allocation being replayed. The optimizer operates on existing GPU parameters, gradients, and optimizer state. This change keeps the capture restrictions on the capturing thread while allowing independent background allocations. It does not add synchronization or make shared-memory races safe. See the [CUDA capture-mode semantics](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-runtime-api/cuda_runtime_api/group__CUDART__STREAM.html#group__CUDART__STREAM_1g9d0535d93a214cbf126835257b16ba85).\n\nRe-enable `hybrid_llama3_proxy_mfsdp_v2_cuda_graph` in both the internal `mr` and GitHub `mr-github` scopes, removing the quarantine associated with #8218. The existing functional test covers full-iteration and optimizer graph capture with MFSDP v2.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Actual functional harness on PR head `b09a550a3`: `run_ci_test.sh` with the configured `ft_launcher`, `N_REPEAT=5`, and `ENABLE_LIGHTWEIGHT_MODE=false` on 8 H100s (Slurm job `6252334`). **5/5 repetitions passed**, each completing all 50 steps. All 250 logged losses exactly match the existing golden values (maximum difference **0**). Both memory checks passed: maximum difference **4,096 bytes**, under **0.000661%**, versus the existing 5% tolerance. Each repetition has one complete TensorBoard loss stream and only `attempt_0`; no crashes or automatic restarts. No race injection or changes to golden values/tolerances. This used the 26.08 development environment specified below.\n- Patched `hybrid_llama3_proxy_mfsdp_v2_cuda_graph`, with real DataLoader pinning deliberately overlapped with optimizer capture: completes all 50 steps; all 50 losses are bit-identical to the existing golden values. The harness retains the first four pinned batches to force a fresh allocation and releases the fifth during optimizer capture. Training uses `torch.distributed.run` without restarts rather than CI's `ft_launcher`.\n- Both full-model checks used the available development container with PyTorch `2.14.0a0+4fdf77b940.nv26.08`, CUDA 13.4, and Transformer Engine `2.19.0+5e52befd`. A separate reduced probe on the 26.09 base runtime reproduced failure with `global` in 3/3 trials and succeeded with `thread_local` in 3/3 trials.\n- `tools/autoformat.sh`: Black, isort, pylint, Ruff, and mypy passed. `git diff --check` passed.\n- The repository recipe parser selects the restored case for `mr`, `mr-github` / `L1`, and merge-group cadence; neither quarantined scope selects it anymore.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nFixes #8218. The controlled reproduction establishes this failure mechanism and the fix. The original CI logs show the matching downstream capture failure but do not trace the first invalidating CUDA API. TensorBoard selection of the first, truncated event file after a successful restart is a separate issue.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n### Pre-checks\n\n- [ ] I have added relevant unit tests.\n- [x] I have restored the existing MFSDP v2 CUDA graph functional test in internal and GitHub CI.\n- [ ] GPU kernel determinism test: not applicable; no kernel is added or changed.\n- [ ] I have added proper typing to my code.\n- [x] I have documented the capture-mode choice in the code and this description.\n- [x] I have run `tools/autoformat.sh` on my PR.\n\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
